{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgApMhVyJtXQ5PEXsuHes","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The job has been running every night; it was failing silently. `launchctl-print.txt` shows `runs = 6` and `last exit code = 1`, one run per night since you loaded it. The error log shows two problems, and the second is why you never heard about the first. Both are fixed; I haven't installed or run anything on your real machine.\n\n1. **`claude` was \"Not logged in\" under launchd.** The job's environment has no `USER`, so the CLI couldn't find its login in the keychain and quit straight away. I added `USER`, `LOGNAME` and `HOME` to the `EnvironmentVariables` in the plist.\n2. **`status=$?` killed the script before it could report.** In zsh, `status` is read-only, so assigning to it ends the script with an error (`nightly-review.zsh:19: read-only variable: status`). That line sat between the `claude` call and the failure notification, so `notify.sh` was never called. It's now `rc=$?`.\n\nI also changed `bin/nightly-review.zsh` in a few other ways:\n- **Catch-all failure message:** if the script dies for any reason it didn't already report, it now sends a failure message.\n- **Prompt on stdin:** the prompt is now piped into `claude -p` instead of passed as a multi-line argument.\n- **Exit 0 isn't enough:** the run counts as failed if the output file is empty or `claude` finished in under 10 seconds.\n- **Logging:** each run writes its duration and the `claude` exit code to the `.err` log.\n\n**Testing:** I ran the script with stand-in `claude` and `notify.sh` in a scratch folder. Each of these sent the right message:\n- `claude` failing with \"Not logged in\"\n- `claude` exiting 0 with no output\n- `claude` exiting 0 too fast\n- a normal 10-second run that read the prompt from stdin\n- the script with the old `status=$?` line put back, where the catch-all sent \"script died\"\n\nThe plist passes `plutil -lint` and the script passes `zsh -n`.\n\n**What you need to do:** copy the files into place, then remove and reload the job and kick it off once. The commands are in `ANSWER.md`. Then check:\n- `last exit code = 0` in `launchctl print`\n- today's `.md` review file exists and isn't empty\n- the run took a plausible time, not a few seconds\n- the \"done\" Telegram message arrived\n\nThen break the script once on purpose and confirm the failure message arrives too. If it still says \"Not logged in\", run `claude` once by hand to log in. Also check that `notify.sh` can read the Telegram bot token from the keychain when launchd runs it; if not, set `TG_BOT_TOKEN` in the plist."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1727,"cache_read_input_tokens":29541,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1727},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"067f53bd-8550-477a-b90e-141b5f1671c8","uuid":"71335b96-9555-41b6-b87c-0b1de452d2f6","timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:36:25.002Z","request_id":"req_011CgApMhFbkTqYKCLZ4uZoB"}
